4. 🛡️ Regularization & Early Stopping
Regularization parameters
Parameter	What it does
max_depth	Limits tree complexity
min_child_weight	Larger value gives a more conservative split
gamma	Minimum loss reduction required to split
reg_lambda	L2 penalty on leaf weights
reg_alpha	L1 penalty on leaf weights
subsample	Fraction of rows per tree
colsample_bytree	Fraction of features per tree

<sub>LightGBM names: num_leaves, min_child_samples, lambda_l2, lambda_l1, bagging_fraction, feature_fraction</sub>

<br>
Early stopping

Stop adding trees when the validation score stops improving.

python
model = XGBClassifier(
    n_estimators=5000,            # set high, let early stopping decide
    learning_rate=0.03,
    eval_metric="aucpr",
    early_stopping_rounds=50,
)

model.fit(X_tr, y_tr, eval_set=[(X_val, y_val)], verbose=False)
print(model.best_iteration)

[!WARNING] Never early-stop on the test set. That is leakage.

[!NOTE] Inside a pipeline, the validation set must be transformed by the already-fitted preprocessor first. Do not apply SMOTE to the validation set.

<br>
Reading learning curves
Train and validation both bad → underfitting. Add depth or trees, or reduce regularization.
Train great, validation worsens → overfitting. Reduce depth, add regularization, use subsampling.
Validation still improving at the end → you need more trees.
