9. 📝 Cheat Sheet
Boosting = sequential trees fitting the negative gradient
Update rule: F_m = F_(m-1) + η · h_m
Recipe: low learning rate + many trees + early stopping
XGBoost = reliable · LightGBM = fast · CatBoost = best with categoricals
Imbalance: scale_pos_weight = neg / pos, or SMOTE inside the fold
Tuning order: trees → structure → sampling → regularization → lower LR
Random search beats grid, Optuna beats random, nested CV gives the honest score
Good AUC does not mean good probabilities. Check the calibration curve
Calibrate on unseen data, then tune the threshold
Never tune or early-stop on the test set, and always keep a baseline
